# dwc-ng — per-developer settings. Copy to .env.local (untracked) and edit.
#
# NOTHING in this project defaults to a particular machine. A checkout with no
# .env.local talks only to the bundled mock, which is the one target that ships
# in this repo. Board addresses, LAN hostnames and passwords are yours.

# --- dev server -------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the default (mock) backend points. Unset = the bundled mock-duet.
#   pnpm --filter @dwc-ng/mock-duet start
# DWC_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8970

# YOUR board, for the in-UI "Real" dev backend. UNSET BY DEFAULT: without it
# the /real proxy routes are not registered at all, so the Real backend is
# simply unavailable rather than quietly pointing somewhere unexpected.
# DWC_REAL=http://your-duet.local

# Hostnames the dev server will accept in the Host header (Vite's DNS-rebinding
# guard). Only needed to reach the dev server from another LAN device by name.
# Comma-separated. localhost always works without this.
# DWC_ALLOWED_HOSTS=my-desktop

# Password for the Real board. Empty = no password. A wrong one fails loudly as
# InvalidPasswordError, which is the intended behaviour.
# VITE_DWC_PASSWORD=

# --- production build -------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED for `pnpm build` — the build refuses without it. Which dialect the
# board you are deploying to speaks. Must match packages/deploy's --mode.
#   rr   standalone RepRapFirmware
#   dsf  Duet 3 + SBC (DuetSoftwareFramework)
# DWC_TRANSPORT=dsf

# Base path when deploying beside stock DWC (see packages/deploy). Default "/".
# DWC_BASE=/ng/

# Extra ORIGINS allowed to make cross-origin requests to the dev server, as a
# comma-separated list of full origins ("http://duet3.nydick.net"). Vite 6+
# blocks cross-origin requests by default (CVE-2025-24010) — necessary here,
# because this server proxies to a printer. localhost and everything in
# DWC_ALLOWED_HOSTS are allowed automatically, on any port.
# DWC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://duet3.nydick.net
